WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.538 --> 00:00:03.135
Here with my faithful Lieutenant Sergey

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.257
and we're off to the Wagah
International Border Crossing.

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:10.347
This is what separates India and Pakistan.

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:11.826
Most likely you've seen it online.

00:00:11.826 --> 00:00:14.988
It's that very theatrical performance

00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:17.045
both nation states put on.

00:00:17.619 --> 00:00:20.068
But what we're gonna
get into here in this video

00:00:20.068 --> 00:00:22.661
is comparing and contrasting

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.313
the two performances.

00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:25.313
So today

00:00:25.794 --> 00:00:27.489
we're gonna get into the Indian side.

00:00:27.489 --> 00:00:29.906
I'm gonna show the Indian side and tomorrow

00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:31.171
the Pakistani side.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:35.893
[motorcycle]

00:00:35.893 --> 00:00:45.247
♪ Indian music ♪

00:00:45.555 --> 00:00:49.333
In 1947, after 300
years of British occupation

00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:52.613
the British left and two
separate countries emerged

00:00:52.613 --> 00:00:53.888
India and Pakistan.

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:58.160
It's got the feeling like we're
going to some sporting event.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.160
How much?

00:00:59.185 --> 00:01:00.275
-50, Sir.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:12.476
♪ Indian music ♪

00:01:12.476 --> 00:01:14.427
It's about a one kilometer walk

00:01:14.427 --> 00:01:15.867
into the crossing.

00:01:16.526 --> 00:01:17.966
First impressions

00:01:18.168 --> 00:01:19.545
feels quite festive

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:22.212
'lotta flags, 'lotta hats, 'lotta shirts

00:01:22.818 --> 00:01:25.844
some food situations and then a massive

00:01:26.502 --> 00:01:29.520
flag through the haze there.

00:01:30.083 --> 00:01:32.197
You love our India?
Me too, brother.

00:01:32.197 --> 00:01:34.464
-Thank you, sir.
-Where's your hat?

00:01:34.975 --> 00:01:37.875
But you got your hand painted.
So that's cool.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.660
Are you guys ready for this?
-Yes.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:42.593
You're ready, you're excited?

00:01:42.622 --> 00:01:43.590
-You are from?

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.042
-USA.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.245 --> 00:01:47.245
-Good, good.

00:01:48.612 --> 00:01:49.867
-One selfie?

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:50.905
-Let's selfie it.

00:01:54.294 --> 00:01:57.908
So I wonder if the Pakistani
side will have the same

00:01:57.908 --> 00:02:01.527
energy, the same fire,
the same friendliness.

00:02:04.352 --> 00:02:06.467
Couldn't record back
there, a lot of barbed wire.

00:02:06.521 --> 00:02:09.185
A lot of security and they're
taking it pretty seriously obviously.

00:02:13.186 --> 00:02:14.568
Go?
Okay.

00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:16.798
Straight?
Okay.

00:02:18.439 --> 00:02:20.826
[Speaking Indian]

00:02:21.128 --> 00:02:22.128
Oh cool.

00:02:22.991 --> 00:02:24.462
Pakistani flag over there.

00:02:24.765 --> 00:02:27.565
Have some stands that are filling up here.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:32.349
I guess this is where
the performance happens.

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:33.586
I'm going over here.

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:36.671
This border ceremony started in 1959

00:02:36.671 --> 00:02:39.320
and has happened daily ever since.

00:02:39.628 --> 00:02:41.698
The border between India and Pakistan is

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:48.067
There are only five crossing points.

00:02:48.365 --> 00:02:53.041
[crowd noise]

00:02:53.762 --> 00:02:56.592
Patriotic music blasts from the speakers

00:02:56.592 --> 00:02:59.156
and organized dance takes over the tarmac.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:05.422
♪ Indian music ♪

00:03:05.896 --> 00:03:08.056
So I look over here to the Pakistani side

00:03:08.056 --> 00:03:11.343
and it just really feels empty and distant.

00:03:11.343 --> 00:03:13.768
♪ Indian music ♪

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:18.543
Here you can see a family
crossing between the two countries.

00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:21.390
A very small percentage
of Indians and Pakistanis

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.916
know what the other side is like.

00:03:23.115 --> 00:03:26.887
It's really not easy for
either nationality to get a visa

00:03:26.887 --> 00:03:28.160
to visit the other country.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:34.117
♪ Indian music ♪

00:03:34.327 --> 00:03:36.199
Though the two
countries are very different

00:03:36.199 --> 00:03:38.969
the border splits the
Punjabi people apart.

00:03:38.969 --> 00:03:43.522
So both sides share linguistic,
culinary, and cultural similarities.

00:03:46.184 --> 00:03:47.982
This video is about the BSF.

00:03:47.982 --> 00:03:50.466
The Indian Border Security Forces.

00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:55.619
The BSF started in the
Indian-Pakistani war of 1965.

00:03:55.619 --> 00:03:58.804
Where the largest tank battle
happened since World War II.

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:00.557
It was a 17 day war.

00:04:00.557 --> 00:04:02.485
Thousands of people died on each side.

00:04:02.485 --> 00:04:06.421
The BSF now has 257,000 personnel

00:04:06.421 --> 00:04:09.573
and it is known as
India's first line of defense.

00:04:09.843 --> 00:04:21.605
♪ patriotic music ♪

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:33.864
♪ military music ♪

00:04:52.631 --> 00:04:56.604
The gates open and the rivals
start with a sportsmanlike handshake.

00:04:59.655 --> 00:05:06.305
♪ military music ♪

00:05:06.612 --> 00:05:07.953
Check out this Indian soldier

00:05:07.953 --> 00:05:11.292
he's a master of combining
gymnastic moves with a militant march.

00:05:11.522 --> 00:05:14.766
♪ military music ♪

00:05:20.065 --> 00:05:22.196
[announcer speaking Indian]

00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:23.500
[crowd responds]

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.656
[announcer continues]

00:05:26.848 --> 00:05:29.565
♪  music continues ♪

00:05:32.793 --> 00:05:35.634
The horns start, faces become more serious.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:36.634
[horns]

00:05:37.112 --> 00:05:40.798
♪ military bugle ♪

00:05:46.895 --> 00:05:49.245
♪ bugles continue ♪

00:05:51.185 --> 00:05:53.818
Yes, the two countries
are political enemies

00:05:53.818 --> 00:05:57.134
but there is a unity in the
way they've choreographed

00:05:57.134 --> 00:05:59.704
this machismo-driven ballet together.

00:06:09.861 --> 00:06:13.189
Today I came from
India in front of us here.

00:06:13.189 --> 00:06:16.454
Went all the way to Lahore, Pakistan.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.152
Which is about 45 minutes away

00:06:19.152 --> 00:06:21.219
and then came back...
[car horn]

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:25.659
and now we're catching
the border from this side.

00:06:25.659 --> 00:06:27.263
to see the other perspective.

00:06:27.655 --> 00:06:29.455
The security coming in here

00:06:30.084 --> 00:06:31.512
was much tighter.

00:06:31.704 --> 00:06:33.289
A lot of checkpoints.

00:06:33.289 --> 00:06:35.519
We put an official in the back of the car.

00:06:35.519 --> 00:06:37.101
The guy I was driving with

00:06:37.101 --> 00:06:38.541
knew the official

00:06:39.088 --> 00:06:40.377
and we put him in the back

00:06:40.377 --> 00:06:42.713
and then we got through all
the checkpoints super quick.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.650
What do you think it's
gonna be like today?

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.820
What is this gonna be like?

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:49.069
-It's gonna be surprising.

00:06:49.369 --> 00:06:51.194
Okay, so here on the Pakistani side

00:06:51.194 --> 00:06:53.031
the approach is very much the same.

00:06:53.031 --> 00:06:57.237
Patriotic music gets louder each
step as I get closer to the border.

00:06:57.512 --> 00:07:01.067
♪ loud music ♪

00:07:12.929 --> 00:07:14.779
The Pakistani stadium is much smaller

00:07:14.779 --> 00:07:17.710
and it's almost to scale of
each country's populations.

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:25.268
[crowd cheering]

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:31.493
Both sides have the same chant of Zindabad.

00:07:31.493 --> 00:07:34.207
Even though I'm just meters away
from where I was the day before

00:07:34.207 --> 00:07:35.732
it feels a world away.

00:07:35.732 --> 00:07:39.013
The colors are different, the clothes
are different, the drum beats harder.

00:07:39.236 --> 00:07:40.265
Thank you, brother.

00:07:40.265 --> 00:07:42.021
[crowd cheering]

00:07:42.218 --> 00:07:45.304
The Rangers are Pakistan's
equivalent of India's BSF.

00:07:45.304 --> 00:07:47.751
There are 25,000 rangers in total.

00:07:47.751 --> 00:07:50.086
So these rangers, from first impression.

00:07:50.086 --> 00:07:52.783
They're much bigger
and more grizzly looking

00:07:52.783 --> 00:07:54.679
than the BSF guys.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.443
The rangers have rockstar-like status

00:07:57.609 --> 00:08:01.232
and there are better chances to
interact with them versus the Indian side.

00:08:03.682 --> 00:08:06.882
Both sides have the ringleaders
to fire up the spectators.

00:08:06.882 --> 00:08:09.682
Different styles but equally as effective.

00:08:09.682 --> 00:08:13.838
[crowd cheering]
♪ patriotic music ♪

00:08:18.632 --> 00:08:21.684
Because of the smaller size of the
stadium it feels much more intimate

00:08:21.684 --> 00:08:22.777
and connected.

00:08:22.777 --> 00:08:24.708
[crowd cheering]

00:08:25.327 --> 00:08:28.138
[announcers speaking]

00:08:44.861 --> 00:08:48.253
The huge bonus on the
Pakistani side is the live drum.

00:08:48.328 --> 00:08:51.113
Two women start the
parade just like the Indian side

00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:54.114
♪ military music ♪

00:08:59.108 --> 00:09:01.204
[crowd cheering]

00:09:05.827 --> 00:09:08.826
[crowd cheers]

00:09:09.406 --> 00:09:11.006
♪ music continues ♪

00:09:13.956 --> 00:09:20.304
[announcer chants and crowd answers]

00:09:22.401 --> 00:09:25.128
I didn't remember seeing
a sword on the Indian side

00:09:25.128 --> 00:09:28.155
but I feel more aggression
from the rangers.

00:09:28.621 --> 00:09:30.061
♪ military music ♪

00:09:36.192 --> 00:09:39.159
If I had to choose between
seeing an angry BSF soldier

00:09:39.159 --> 00:09:41.088
or a ranger in a dark alleyway

00:09:41.088 --> 00:09:44.163
I'd definitely prefer the BSF soldier.

00:09:44.396 --> 00:09:46.953
Look, both could easily
dismantle me in two seconds

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:50.270
but the ranger's size and
intensity are unmatched.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:54.308
[crowd gets louder]

00:09:55.863 --> 00:09:56.863
[air horns]

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.862
[cheering]

00:09:59.479 --> 00:10:00.919
♪ military music ♪

00:10:15.301 --> 00:10:18.937
They're true performers with
little details like mustache twirling.

00:10:18.937 --> 00:10:20.537
[announcer shouting]

00:10:21.228 --> 00:10:24.242
&lt;He's sitting down now but
he's gonna come through.

00:10:25.604 --> 00:10:28.735
Pride towards national
identity feel equally as strong

00:10:28.735 --> 00:10:30.334
on both sides of the border.

00:10:31.396 --> 00:10:32.996
♪ music continues ♪

00:10:37.324 --> 00:10:38.924
[clapping in rhythm]

00:10:43.467 --> 00:10:47.733
♪ military bugles ♪

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:53.238
Whatever side I was on,
 it connected me more with that country.

00:10:53.238 --> 00:10:56.613
So if someone doesn't have
the chance to sit on the other side

00:10:56.613 --> 00:10:58.875
then it feels like a distant world away.

00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:00.395
♪ bugles continue ♪

00:11:00.969 --> 00:11:02.169
[loud cheering]

00:11:09.945 --> 00:11:11.897
Even though there is that serious rivalry

00:11:11.897 --> 00:11:14.195
and distrust between the countries

00:11:14.195 --> 00:11:16.476
there is also that unity in the celebration

00:11:16.476 --> 00:11:19.190
as each side needs the other to perform.

00:11:19.395 --> 00:11:20.915
♪ patriotic music ♪

00:11:31.132 --> 00:11:32.332
[whistle blows]

00:11:36.411 --> 00:11:39.097
I can tell you from my
experience that the locals are open

00:11:39.097 --> 00:11:42.730
hospitable and friendly
on both sides of this divided

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:45.214
and very entertaining border.

